0.14 What Comes Next?
While \(\varepsilon\)-greedy action selection guarantees asymptotic exploration, its randomised choices are indiscriminate: it explores promising and dismal alternatives with equal likelihood. In Season 1, Episode 02: Curious, but Clever, we formulate guided, directed exploration mechanisms: - Optimism in the Face of Uncertainty: Initial value biases that encourage transient, self-terminating exploration. - Upper Confidence Bound (UCB): Quantifying epistemic uncertainty via concentration bounds to attain logarithmic regret \(\mathcal{O}(\log T)\). - Gradient Bandits: Learning continuous action preference probabilities through softmax stochastic gradient ascent.





